course: dictionary
lesson: 8396
title: Rue: regret, a herb, or a French street
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word rue has three different meanings, so check the sentence to find the right one. Look for clues: a feeling, a plant, or a place.
explain: As a verb, rue means to feel sorry about something and wish it had not happened. «You'll rue the day you crossed me!» means the villain will be sorry later, when it is too late.
explain: As a noun, rue is a strong-smelling herb with yellow flowers and bluish leaves, used long ago as a medicine. In French, «rue» means street, so «la deuxième rue à droite» means the second street on the right.
explain: To choose the right meaning, swap your idea into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If someone is sorry about a choice, it is rue the verb. If there is a sign or a town, it is probably the French word.
fact: «Rue» as a verb means to feel sorry about something and wish it had not happened.
fact: The verb forms are rue, rues, rued and ruing, as in «He rued his choice.»
fact: «Rue» as a noun is a plant with strong-smelling leaves and yellow flowers, once used as a medicine.
fact: In French, «rue» means street, as in «rue de la Paix».
fact: Say the French word with a tight, rounded mouth, a bit like «roo»; in English it is not a word for street.
exercise: «You'll rue the day you crossed me!» What does rue mean here? | To laugh loudly at a joke | To find something lost | To grow yellow flowers | *To feel sorry about something and wish it had not happened
exercise: Long ago, rue was used for what? | To keep birds away | To make paper | To shine like a lamp | *As a medicine
exercise: «Tout droit, puis la deuxième rue à droite, à côté de l'église.» What does rue mean in this French sentence? | River | Church | Bridge | *Street
test: «He rued the day he lost his best friend.» Which feeling does rued show? | *Sorrow and regret | Joy at winning a prize | Pride in a new bike | Surprise at a loud noise
test: Which sentence uses rue as a plant? | We walked down the rue to the café. | *The garden had a bush of rue with yellow flowers. | You will rue this if you lie to me. | The rued boy ran home.
exam: A friend says rue always means sad, because a French sign says «rue de la Paix». What is the best answer? | The sign is wrong, because rue never means anything | *Rue is French for street here, so on the sign it means street, not sadness | Rue is a plant, so it means sad | Rue means sad in every language
